From 57e0f60a7b332c21efefb184b7843dcefb209c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyxia <72890320+tyxia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 14:45:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tls: Remove deprecated enforce_rsa_key_usage and
 was_key_usage_invalid (#45326)

BoringSSL will remove the `SSL_set_enforce_rsa_key_usage` and
`SSL_was_key_usage_invalid` API.

enfore_ras_key_usage has been default to True in Envoy for several
months and was_key_usage_invaild stas has been in Envoy for 2+ years.
Both of them aim to capture invalid key usage, no issues and report has
been reported so far. Thus, we assume it is safe to deprecate the
related code in Envoy as BoringSSL will remove those APIs anyway.

